{"study_accession":"PRJNA1152316","secondary_study_accession":"SRP534540","title":"High IGHV intraclonal diversification identifies CLL with good prognosis, features of anergy and specific T-cell profile","description":"Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) with IGHV gene identity >=98% (U-CLL) experienced a worse prognosis respect to CLL with IGHV gene identity <98% (M-CLL). Moreover, CLL cells may exhibit ongoing mutations in IGHV genes, a phenomenon known as intraclonal diversification (ID). Through an original bioinformatic workflow for NGS data, we dichotomize cases with different ID levels into IDhigh and IDlow in CLL (n=983). Bioinformatic analysis of deconvoluted cell fractions from bulk RNASeq of IDlow, vs. IDhigh M-CLL (n=18) highlighted features of anergy in IDhigh M-CLL cells. When circumscribed to the T-cell component of IDhigh vs. IDlow M-CLL, bioinformatic analysis identified, both in CD8 and CD4 cell fractions of IDhigh M-CLL, an enrichment in T-cell activation pathways, induction of immunological synapsis-associated pathways and T-cell effectors functions.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN43359830","study_accession":"PRJNA1152316","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"TS22","description":"TS22","sex":"not applicable","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-09-21","attributes":[["isolate","=B13&\"_R1\""],["age","56"],["biomaterial_provider","Clinical and experimental oncohematology"],["collection_date","2003-03-01"],["geo_loc_name","Italy"],["sex","not applicable"],["tissue","PBMC"],["cell_line","not applicable"],["cell_subtype","not applicable"],["cell_type","PBMC"],["culture_collection","not applicable"],["dev_stage","not applicable"],["disease","chronic lymphocytic leukemia"],["disease_stage","not applicable"],["ethnicity","not applicable"],["health_state","not applicable"],["karyotype","not applicable"],["phenotype","not applicable"],["p